{"type":"assistant","uuid":"bfe05d67-ccdd-4ca6-9513-b1bb9502e7d4","session_id":"b8699ab0-01de-4568-96a8-16d7259edfdf","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"bfe05d67-ccdd-4ca6-9513-b1bb9502e7d4","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The exploration agent confirmed my analysis and fix is correct. The bug is that `openNoteEditorForCurrentlySelectedNote()` only passes the first selected card, and `NoteEditor` already has partial support for multi-select via `EXTRA_NOTE_IDS` but CardBrowser never wired it up. My patch addresses exactly this.\n\nLet me also update the `hasSelectedSingleNoteId()` check - currently it hides the Edit button when more than 50 cards are selected, but for batch type change, we should allow editing multiple notes as long as each card belongs to a different note (or at least support it). Actually, looking at the code more carefully, the `hasSelectedSingleNoteId()` check is there to ensure we only enable Edit when all selected cards belong to the same note. This makes sense for the old single-note editing behavior.\n\nFor the multi-select fix, we actually want to enable Edit when cards belong to multiple notes (to do batch type change). So we should modify the `hasSelectedSingleNoteId()` check or create a new method. Let me think about this...\n\nActually, re-reading the bug description: \"Browser → select the two new cards → Edit → try to change the type\". The two cards are in the first type, and the user wants to move them to the second type. These two cards likely belong to different notes (or could be the same note if it's a two-card type like \"Basic\").\n\nThe `hasSelectedSingleNoteId()` heuristic returns false when more than 50 cards are selected to avoid overhead. For ≤50 cards, it returns true only if all cards belong to the same note. If they belong to different notes, it returns false.\n\nThis means for the current code, the Edit button is only visible when ALL selected cards belong to the same note. For the multi-select type change to work properly, we need to allow editing notes that belong to multiple different notes too.\n\nLet me update the `hasSelectedSingleNoteId()` method to support both cases:\n1. All cards belong to one note → edit single note (existing behavior)\n2. Cards belong to multiple notes → batch edit all notes (new behavior)\n\nActually, looking at this more carefully, the Edit button visibility check `mActionBarMenu.findItem(R.id.action_edit_note).setVisible(hasSelectedSingleNoteId());` only allows editing when all cards are from the same note. For batch type change across different notes, we need to change this.\n\nLet me update the fix to also address this visibility constraint.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
